quiet.md #12: synthetic italics for faces without an italic

When italic text asks for a family with no italic face (PingFang), or CoreText
falls back to such a face, use an "oblique twin" FontId of the upright face
that is rasterized with WebKit's synthetic 14° shear; its glyph bounds are
widened to match. Chinese italics now lean as they do in a browser; before
they were drawn upright.

